---

Troubleshooting Tips

If the LEDs do not work:

- Check the Arduino power supply.
- Verify Pin 16 is connected to 5V.
- Verify Pin 8 is connected to GND.
- Ensure Pin 13 (OE) is connected to GND.
- Ensure Pin 10 (MR) is connected to 5V.
- Check LED polarity.
- Verify all resistors are connected properly.
- Confirm the push button is wired correctly.
- Inspect the breadboard for loose connections.

---

Conclusion

This project demonstrates the practical use of the 74HC595 Shift Register for GPIO expansion, push button interfacing, and LED pattern generation. It provides a strong foundation in Arduino programming, digital electronics, and embedded systems while showing how serial-to-parallel communication can simplify hardware design.
